    "def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space with inner product linear in its first argument ([[def-hilbert-space]], [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]). Write $\\mathcal B(H)$ for the bounded linear operators on $H$ ([[def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators]]); for $M\\in\\mathcal B(H)$, $M^*$ is its Hilbert adjoint, characterized by $\\langle Mx,y\\rangle=\\langle x,M^*y\\rangle$ ([[def-hilbert-space-adjoint]]).\n\nA **finite bounded Kraus instrument datum** on $H$ consists of an integer $m\\ge1$, integers $q_a\\ge0$ for $a=1,\\ldots,m$, and bounded operators $M_{a,r}\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ for $r=1,\\ldots,q_a$. It is **normalized** when\n\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^{m}\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r}=I_H.$$\n\nEmpty inner sums are zero. For each outcome $a$, define its outcome operator and operation by\n\n$$E_a:=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}^*M_{a,r},\\qquad \\mathcal J_a(X):=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*\\quad(X\\in\\mathcal B(H)).$$\n\nThese formulas take values in $\\mathcal B(H)$: each composition is bounded since $\\|M_{a,r}XM_{a,r}^*x\\|\\le\\|M_{a,r}\\|\\,\\|X\\|\\,\\|M_{a,r}^*\\|\\,\\|x\\|$, and the sums are finite. This definition specifies only the displayed finite Kraus form; it is not a representation theorem for arbitrary instruments and does not assert that an apparatus realizes these data."
    ],
    "lem-qft-finite-instrument-normalization": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ carry a normalized finite bounded Kraus instrument datum as defined in [[def-qft-finite-bounded-kraus-instrument]], and let $\\rho$ be a density operator on $H$: a self-adjoint positive trace-class operator with $\\operatorname{tr}\\rho=1$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-density-and-scalar-spectral-probability]], [[def-trace-class-operator]], [[def-trace-of-a-trace-class-operator]], [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]). For each outcome $a$, put $p_a:=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))$. Then each $E_a$ is an effect ($E_a\\ge0$ and $I_H-E_a\\ge0$), each $\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is positive trace class, and\n\n$$p_a=\\operatorname{tr}(\\mathcal J_a(\\rho))=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_a)\\in[0,1],\\qquad \\sum_{a=1}^{m}p_a=1.$$\n\nThe nonselective output $\\sum_a\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)$ is a density operator. If $p_a>0$, the normalized conditional state $\\rho_a:=\\mathcal J_a(\\rho)/p_a$ is a density operator; when $p_a=0$, this normalized update is undefined. For a unit vector $\\psi\\in H$, the rank-one density operator $\\rho=T_{\\psi,\\psi}$ has outcome probability $p_a=\\sum_{r=1}^{q_a}\\|M_{a,r}\\psi\\|^2$. These are conditional mathematical identities; they do not assert that an apparatus realizes the instrument or supply a physical measurement postulate."
    ],
    "cex-qft-formal-factorial-series": [
      null
    ]
  }
